From bcd6465ed236470677a6885901f5c711d565dccd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shiro <build@shiro>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 07:40:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Shiro: small callees compile into their caller's region;
 bigger TLBs and a one-compare TLB check

A region now takes in the whole of a small function it calls directly
(every block its direct branches reach: at most 6 blocks of 64
instructions, its own calls likewise two levels down), and a ret whose
address is one of the region's return points goes on there inside the
region. A function that doesn't fit is left out entirely: running part
of it in the caller's region would leave the region in the middle of it,
which costs more than calling it through WjCall. BLINK_WJIT_OFF bit 21
turns this off.

The JIT's translation caches (Machine::wjr/wjw) grow from 256 to 4096
pages and FindPageTableEntry's TLB from 32 to 1024: native Claude Code's
heap thrashed both (TLB refills were ~3 s of a 50 s start). A cache hit
is one compare: the entry for an access's first page has to hold the page
of its last byte, which a page-crossing access's doesn't; the entry keeps
host page - guest page, so the host address is one add.

SHIRO_BLINK_PROFILE also writes the guest instructions run in compiled
code per region (SHIRO_BLINK_PROFILE_REGIONS=n lists n), region entries
by path (the interpreter, WjExecute's chain, WjCall) and TLB resets.
---
